KZ2 patch 6101 (2026-11-25): SPU poll counters, step 0 of the SPU poll backoff work
(measure first, then patch). KZ2_SPU_POLL_STATS=1 counts, process-wide, the policy-module poll
answers at SPURS_PM_SELECT_WORKLOAD_LS (all, and the plain "keep running" answer) and the GETLLARs (all; those on the
same line as the thread's previous GETLLAR; those whose 128 bytes are also unchanged since that read, i.e. the re-reads
a backoff such as RetroRemakes' RR_SPU_LLAR_PARK_US would park), and prints `[spu-poll] 10.0 s: pm-poll N/s (continue
N/s) getllar N/s same-line N/s unchanged N/s` every 10 s. Read together with KZ3_SPURS_CPU=1's [spurs-cpu] lines (the
HLE kernel threads' CPU ms/s) to see whether idle polling burns host cores. Off by default: one cached flag test at
each point, nothing counted. Counters only, no behaviour change. RetroRemakes Killzone 2 1.2 patch 7007 (RemakerGamee,
MIT) was read for what to count; no code taken from it.

--- a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
@@ -83,6 +83,39 @@
 #endif
